From b2453e71fa02ebf4ac81848cf9e13f7b86a2fef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:40:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] LV8: level packs (BRPK v1): format, writer
 tools/packbreach.py, platform manifest, core reader and tests

core/include/doomo/breachpack.h + core/src/breachpack.c: platform-neutral reader (bp_head / bp_open validate
header, section table, limits, overlaps, sizes, crc; bp_load / bp_load_mode / bp_bin_load build a DoomoMapDef +
DoomoMapExt in a caller arena, no allocation, no static state, explicit field reads). tools/packbreach.py writes
packs (cells LZ with the PS1 codec, raw where smaller) and BREACH.BIN (24-entry directory, sector aligned).
core/data/maps/platforms.txt is the manifest (7 GBA levels `gba yes`); mapc guards manifest levels so the PS1
never links them and the GBA only the 7. 28 C tests (round trips of t2_script, t3_kit, t4_env, t2_tables,
t2_swap_toggle, t8_bank and two shipped maps; every refusal) and 29 Python tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cxE5CiE8LkNQXc6Au3
